    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, acceptance tests green).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe feature: `POST /api/owners` accepts an optional `registrationDate`; when omitted the server defaults it to today, and it's returned as an ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` string.\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the shared `OwnerFields` schema, so it's both accepted on input and echoed on output. The generator produces a `LocalDate` DTO field, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`, and MapStruct maps it automatically (no mapper edits).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field with a plain getter/setter and a `@PrePersist` hook that defaults it to `LocalDate.now()` only when null (so a supplied date is preserved and the default is persisted at registration time).\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column (the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`) and extended the positional seed inserts to match.\n- **`db/h2`, `db/postgres`, `db/mysql` schemas** \u2014 added the same column so the other supported profiles keep working (their seed inserts use named columns, so no data changes were needed there).\n\n## Structural-impact notes\n\n- No existing method was modified \u2014 the controller, service, and mapper are untouched. The default logic lives in one tiny new `@PrePersist` method (CC 2), and the new accessors are CC 1, so the per-function cost stays minimal.\n- MapStruct auto-mapping meant the mapper interface didn't need editing, avoiding cost in a class with derived-field expressions.\n- The Java change is confined to a single file (`Owner.java`); the rest are declarative SQL/YAML.",
